event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"item_id":"rs_342883","output_index":0,"sequence_number":272,"summary_index":0,"text":"The implementation seems mostly correct. However, some issues: The route for opening project uses `/projects/\u003cid\u003e.html` which matches the requirement: \"Opening a project navigates to `/projects/\u003cproject-id\u003e`\". The spec says path `/projects/\u003cproject-id\u003e` without .html. Our implementation uses .html. That may cause mismatch. Should be `/projects/\u003cid\u003e` (no extension). Also need to serve project page for that route.\n\nAlso need to ensure data-testid on each row.\n\nHealth endpoint correct.\n\nNeed to ensure static serving works for `/projects/\u003cid\u003e`.\n\nOur serveStatic only serves `/projects/... .html`. So need to adjust to serve `/projects/\u003cid\u003e` and serve project.html.\n\nAlso need to ensure server binds to 0.0.0.0 at PORT env default 8080.\n\nThat's fine.\n\nWe also need to ensure DB path env variable DB_PATH used.\n\nNow need to adjust server.js to serve project page for `/projects/:id` without .html. Also client should navigate accordingly.\n\nUpdate client: openBtn should set location.href = `/projects/${proj.id}`.\n\nUpdate server static serving: if pathname matches `/projects/\u003cid\u003e` then serve project.html.\n\nAlso need to adjust project.html script to parse ID from URL path without .html.\n\nModify project.html accordingly.\n\nNow implement changes.\n\n","type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done"}

event: response.output_item.done
data: {"item":{"encrypted_content":"The implementation seems mostly correct. However, some issues: The route for opening project uses `/projects/\u003cid\u003e.html` which matches the requirement: \"Opening a project navigates to `/projects/\u003cproject-id\u003e`\". The spec says path `/projects/\u003cproject-id\u003e` without .html. Our implementation uses .html. That may cause mismatch. Should be `/projects/\u003cid\u003e` (no extension). Also need to serve project page for that route.\n\nAlso need to ensure data-testid on each row.\n\nHealth endpoint correct.\n\nNeed to ensure static serving works for `/projects/\u003cid\u003e`.\n\nOur serveStatic only serves `/projects/... .html`. So need to adjust to serve `/projects/\u003cid\u003e` and serve project.html.\n\nAlso need to ensure server binds to 0.0.0.0 at PORT env default 8080.\n\nThat's fine.\n\nWe also need to ensure DB path env variable DB_PATH used.\n\nNow need to adjust server.js to serve project page for `/projects/:id` without .html. Also client should navigate accordingly.\n\nUpdate client: openBtn should set location.href = `/projects/${proj.id}`.\n\nUpdate server static serving: if pathname matches `/projects/\u003cid\u003e` then serve project.html.\n\nAlso need to adjust project.html script to parse ID from URL path without .html.\n\nModify project.html accordingly.\n\nNow implement changes.\n\n","id":"rs_342883","summary":[{"text":"The implementation seems mostly correct. However, some issues: The route for opening project uses `/projects/\u003cid\u003e.html` which matches the requirement: \"Opening a project navigates to `/projects/\u003cproject-id\u003e`\". The spec says path `/projects/\u003cproject-id\u003e` without .html. Our implementation uses .html. That may cause mismatch. Should be `/projects/\u003cid\u003e` (no extension). Also need to serve project page for that route.\n\nAlso need to ensure data-testid on each row.\n\nHealth endpoint correct.\n\nNeed to ensure static serving works for `/projects/\u003cid\u003e`.\n\nOur serveStatic only serves `/projects/... .html`. So need to adjust to serve `/projects/\u003cid\u003e` and serve project.html.\n\nAlso need to ensure server binds to 0.0.0.0 at PORT env default 8080.\n\nThat's fine.\n\nWe also need to ensure DB path env variable DB_PATH used.\n\nNow need to adjust server.js to serve project page for `/projects/:id` without .html. Also client should navigate accordingly.\n\nUpdate client: openBtn should set location.href = `/projects/${proj.id}`.\n\nUpdate server static serving: if pathname matches `/projects/\u003cid\u003e` then serve project.html.\n\nAlso need to adjust project.html script to parse ID from URL path without .html.\n\nModify project.html accordingly.\n\nNow implement changes.\n\n","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},"output_index":0,"sequence_number":273,"type":"response.output_item.done"}

